Performance work adapts native-JavaScript rendering reuse, retained-buffer and
binary-heap navigation patterns from QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS, Apache-2.0, at
1f965f4e5b6669de0f954e3a39b11aa679e56720. Its rendering reuse credits the
invariant/signature concepts in QSOLKCB/OPT at
7556dd36acd53ed3ed538fd03b1db44e5c1ec869. No Wonderbuild or GPL donor source
is copied. CorpoWars retains its original projection, geometry and route rules.
See docs/PERFORMANCE.md for provenance, exactness and measurement limits.

The tactical upgrade also adapts changed-range vertex uploads from
QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS modules/render-webgl/index.js at
93ace342c11e2427ad82920c8965f16e91518fb7, and retained static/dynamic batch
separation from QSOLKCB/CorpoWars3d src/renderer.js at
8e86066686a575402ee2818378f1ec9323fb9ee6 (both Apache-2.0).
These are local adaptations; neither repository is a runtime dependency.
The default projection is preserved; optional quarter-turn views add original
camera transforms and rear building faces. See docs/TACTICAL_UPGRADE.md.
